{{!-- ONE SEASON ON A SIDEWAYS TIMELINE.

      The slide-deck shape: one axis line across the page, a node on it per season, and that
      season's cards hanging off the node on a short stalk -- above the line for one season, below
      it for the next (`above`, alternated by the view model), so neighbours never crowd each other.

      ⚠ THE NODE COMES FIRST IN THE DOM, whichever side its cards hang on. The grid places the cards
      in the top or the bottom row; a screen reader and the Tab key read the season's name and then
      what happened in it, in that order, every time.

      The axis itself is drawn by the node (a rule across its whole column), so the line stays
      continuous from season to season with nothing measured in script. Every node carries its own
      year chip (the shared heading), and the season that OPENS a year (`startsYear`) is marked on
      the axis as well, so the years read at a glance along the line.

      Context: one period view-model (timeline-view.js#periodVM). --}}
<li class="stonetop-timeline-hperiod {{#if above}}stonetop-timeline-hperiod--above{{else}}stonetop-timeline-hperiod--below{{/if}}{{#if startsYear}} stonetop-timeline-hperiod--year-start{{/if}}" data-period="{{key}}">
	<div class="stonetop-timeline-hnode">
		<div class="stonetop-timeline-hhead">
			{{> "stonetop.timeline-period-head"}}
		</div>
	</div>
	<ol class="stonetop-timeline-cards stonetop-timeline-hcards">
		{{#each entries}}{{> "stonetop.timeline-card"}}{{/each}}
	</ol>
</li>
